units=[
dict(id='R1',statement='Exact sector and printed PC = ordinary convexity, with rational coefficients distinguished from literal integral-slope PA.',proof='Work on X=R^d with its full standard rational affine structure, d>=1, and positive constant top-cycle weight w. A finite balanced full-dimensional decomposition of the whole affine space has the same weight on adjacent top cells by primitive codimension-one balance, so this is also the exact full-support positive balanced category after refining. For a continuous function, printed PC implies ordinary LOCAL convexity even if the fixed carrier must be refined rather than coarsened. Around x in the relative interior of a face tau, a small ball meets only cells incident to tau. Rational centers in tau are dense. Rational small opposite displacements satisfying the incident-cell inequalities approximate every real opposite displacement, because these are finite rational polyhedral cone constraints. Printed PCC with endpoints q-h,q+h and real weights 1/2 then gives the local midpoint inequality; continuity passes rational centers/endpoints to x and arbitrary sufficiently small displacements. Continuous local midpoint convexity gives local convexity by dyadic weights. Restricting to any compact line segment and partitioning it into finitely many such neighborhoods makes secant slopes nondecreasing across the partition, hence gives global convexity. Ordinary convexity implies every printed PCC inequality. This argument does not authorize coarsening a required carrier or assume all original distant endpoint tuples are themselves legal. No analogous ambient-convex conclusion is asserted on branched or merely embedded supports. The reference gamma is continuous convex finite PA with RATIONAL affine coefficients and positive growth gamma>=a|x|-b, a>0. Actual gamma stays fixed. Generated rational-slope PA functions belong to S272 explicit real/rational-denominator primitive sector after denominator clearing. This is NOT a density assertion inside the literal integral-slope-only category, and NOT an arbitrary irrational-reference theorem.'),
dict(id='R2',statement='A finite lower-semicontinuous convex function on a compact polytope is continuous on the entire polytope.',proof='Let P be a compact polytope and g:P->R finite, convex and lower semicontinuous. If v_i are its finitely many vertices, convexity gives g<=B=max_i g(v_i). Fix x in P. Write P in its affine span by finitely many inequalities l_i>=0. Choose r>0 smaller than every positive slack l_i(x)/(2||dl_i||); zero covectors cause no restriction. For y in P sufficiently close to x, t=|y-x|/r<1 and z=x+(y-x)/t satisfy every active inequality (because y does) and every inactive inequality by the slack bound. Thus z in P and y=(1-t)x+t z. Hence g(y)<=g(x)+t(B-g(x)), so limsup_{y->x}g(y)<=g(x). Lower semicontinuity supplies liminf>=g(x). The degenerate zero-dimensional case is immediate. This proves full relative continuity; compactness makes it uniform. It does not use the false assertion that arbitrary convex functions are continuous at boundary points without lower semicontinuity.'),
dict(id='R3',statement='Full global rational-PA regularization of EVERY continuous convex f with bounded difference from this actual rational reference.',proof='Write gamma(x)=max_i(p_i.x+b_i) with p_i,b_i rational; this finite supporting-plane representation follows directly from finite PA convexity. Put P=conv{p_i}. Positive growth makes P full-dimensional and containing a positive ball. If |f-gamma|<=C, Fenchel conjugates satisfy gamma*-C<=f*<=gamma*+C on their common domain. Separation shows dom gamma*=P: outside P some direction makes p.x-gamma(x) tend to infinity, while for p=sum alpha_i p_i the bound gamma(x)>=p.x+sum alpha_i b_i gives gamma*(p)<=-min b_i. Evaluation at zero gives its finite lower bound. Therefore f* is finite on compact rational P, infinite outside, convex and lower semicontinuous. R2 makes it uniformly continuous on all P. Finite-dimensional supporting hyperplanes give f=f**; explicitly a support plane at each x exists by separation of the closed convex epigraph, so the supremum of support planes equals f, not an unproved singular-envelope regularization.\nTriangulate P with rational vertices and use repeated barycentric subdivision. A simplex of dimension<=d shrinks by at most d/(d+1): barycenters of nested nonempty faces A subset B differ by at most (|B|-|A|)/|B| times the parent diameter; all vertices of a child simplex correspond to a nested chain. Thus meshes tend to zero and every vertex stays rational. Let V_n contain all vertices of the n-th triangulation, including every original vertex of P. Choose rational numbers r_{n,p} approximating f*(p) uniformly within eta_n->0, and define g_n(x)=max_{p in V_n}(p.x-r_{n,p}). This is genuinely finite rational PA on rational geometry, continuous convex/printed PC, with recession support function h_P exactly equal to gamma infinity.\nFor the unrounded values, q_n(x)=max_{p in V_n}(p.x-f*(p))<=f(x). If p in P lies in a mesh simplex with vertices p_j and p=sum alpha_j p_j, then p.x-f*(p)<=sum alpha_j[p_j.x-f*(p_j)]+sum alpha_j[f*(p_j)-f*(p)]<=q_n(x)+omega(mesh_n). Taking the supremum over p proves 0<=f-q_n<=omega(mesh_n) at EVERY x in R^d, independently of |x|. Rounding changes q_n by at most eta_n globally. Thus ||g_n-f||_infinity<=omega(mesh_n)+eta_n->0, and all g_n have one fixed bound relative to the ACTUAL gamma. They lie in its finite operator domain BEFORE any measure is assigned to f. Choose a subsequence with error<=2^-n; then g_n+4*2^-n is nonincreasing, lies above f, and tends to f at every point. This proves actual global-uniform/decreasing primitive regularization and f in S272 genuine D_R(gamma), rather than assigning an operator by inverse or by an unknown local limit.'),
dict(id='R4',statement='Finite rational-PA obstacles have genuinely finite rational-PA convex envelopes with this same reference.',proof='Let u be continuous finite rational PA with compact support and |u|<=C. F=gamma+u is finite rational PA, possibly nonconvex, and gamma-C<=F<=gamma+C. Refine its carrier with gamma so F is affine on each rational cell. Each cell is pointed: an affine gamma on a cell containing a full line cannot satisfy positive growth at both ends. The epigraph of F on each cell is a rational pointed polyhedron, generated by finitely many rational vertices and rays, including the vertical ray. The closed convex hull of their finite union is therefore the rational polyhedron Q=conv(all vertex generators)+cone(all ray generators). This finite generator identity follows by convexly combining the finite cell representations; conversely any conical generator is a recession limit of convex combinations in the union. Finite-dimensional polyhedral cones generated by finitely many vectors are closed after removing lineality and using their finite faces; this is the same elementary rational-cone elimination framework already proved in S272.\nQ contains epi(gamma+C), is contained in epi(gamma-C), and is upward closed. It is epi(q) for a finite convex rational PA q, with |q-gamma|<=C. It is the largest convex minorant of F: every finite continuous convex minorant has closed convex epigraph containing epi F and hence Q, so it is <=q; and q<=F. To identify the unrestricted printed envelope, use the ENTIRE accepted R230 statement with all its full-support/positive-growth qualifications: the actual envelope p=P_gamma(u) is continuous printed PC, hence ordinary convex by R1, so p<=q. Conversely q is a genuine continuous PC minorant with the correct same-reference bound, hence q<=p. Thus q=p. An individual unrestricted printed-PC competitor need NOT be assumed continuous or ordinary convex at irrational points; the accepted envelope identification, not that false implication, supplies this step. It belongs to the original finite primitive domain before its raw MA is formed. No such finite-envelope assertion is made for a branched support or for a reference whose coefficients are irrational.'),
dict(id='R5',statement='Every flat PC jet has zero raw atom on the full affine support, at every rational point and EVERY rational tangent refinement.',proof='Fix any rational point and any finite rational refinement. A convex finite PA germ h at that point, after subtracting its value, is max of finitely many active real linear gradients, so its subgradient set is their convex hull. If a nontrivial printed flat relation is given by nonzero rational tangent vectors b_i and positive real alpha_i with sum alpha_i b_i=0 and sum alpha_i h(b_i)=0, then for every subgradient p, each h(b_i)-p.b_i>=0 and their positively weighted sum is zero. Thus p.b_i=h(b_i) for every active i and every p. Choose one nonzero rational b=b_i and one p0 in the subgradient polytope. The germ h-p0.x is invariant along R b, since all its linear gradients annihilate b. The common linear part has zero primitive derivative on EVERY balanced intermediate signed cycle.\nTake a product rational fan in the quotient by the saturated rational line R b. The full top-cycle [R^d] of weight w and every cycle produced by successive raw primitive derivatives of the invariant germ retain this lineality. Indeed cells/faces and the derivative data pull back from the quotient, and the inward saturated primitive normal calculation changes only quotient coordinates; balancing removes any linear contribution. This is a direct unit-by-unit primitive calculation, including signed and zero intermediate cycles, not an ordinary nonsaturated normal formula. A nonzero finite zero-dimensional fan cycle cannot have a nonzero lineality direction. After d derivatives the cycle is therefore zero. Subdivision invariance in S272 gives the same zero raw atom on the original refinement. This proves the full quantified flat-jet condition, without replacing all refinements by one fan, and without invoking an unproved Alexandrov-volume identity. S272 finite-PA contact iff now applies to EVERY actual finite-PA measured envelope in R4.'),
dict(id='R6',statement='Bounded local-uniform obstacles imply bounded local-uniform actual convex envelopes; explicit tail estimate.',proof='Set H=gamma+c>=0 proper. The actual convex envelope of F=gamma+u is the infimum of expected F under finite barycentric probabilities with barycenter x, including the no-op delta_x. This follows directly: that infimum is convex, bounded between gamma-C and F, and every convex minorant is bounded above by it by Jensen. Its finiteness makes it continuous. R230 identifies the unrestricted envelope with this convex roof exactly as in R4: the actual envelope is continuous PC and hence convex, and the roof itself is an eligible PC minorant. Rational endpoints suffice in the printed problem, because continuity and rational enclosing simplices approximate any finite configuration while maintaining the exact real barycenter; or ordinary convexity can be used after R1. These probabilities are ordinary convex/PCC coefficients, NOT MA measures.\nIf ||u||,||v||<=C, every epsilon-optimal probability nu for u has int H dnu<=H(x)+2C+epsilon by P_u(x)<=gamma(x)+C and -u<=C. Hence nu{H>R}<=(H(x)+2C+epsilon)/R. Evaluate the same probability for v, let epsilon decrease to zero, and reverse u/v to obtain |P_u(x)-P_v(x)|<=sup_{H<=R}|u-v|+2C(H(x)+2C)/R. This is uniform on every compact set of x. Thus uniformly bounded obstacles converging locally uniformly, including nets, have locally uniformly convergent ACTUAL envelopes, with the same relative bound C. It asserts no global uniform density in C_b.'),
dict(id='R7',statement='Localized mixed-measure estimate on the EXISTING genuine completion and its all-bounded-relative local-uniform continuity.',proof='For a compact rational PA test psi, S272 constructs two genuine same-gamma auxiliaries with signed difference epsilon eta_psi psi. On finite relative PA tuples a,b, telescope their mixed product and use the bounded raw integration-by-parts identity to write each term as int(a_i-b_i) D_psi Z_i. Locality makes this signed measure supported in supp psi; its total variation is at most L_psi=2M/(epsilon eta_psi), independently of the tuple. Therefore |int psi[MA(a)-MA(b)]|<=L_psi sum_i sup_{supp psi}|a_i-b_i|. Pass global-uniform finite PA approximants for each of TWO already completed tuples to retain the estimate on D_R(gamma). No new domain is defined.\nR3 establishes D-membership of all the convex endpoints needed here BEFORE this application. Local-uniform convergence of such tuples gives convergence on every compact PA test. Compact ordinary continuous tests can be uniformly approximated by compact rational-PA tests, and all positive outputs have raw mass M, giving vague convergence. On any fixed relative-bound family, the preexisting S272 proper rational-reference height bound gives int H0 MA<=K_C for EVERY mixed tuple, hence tail<=K_C/R on its compact sublevels. Cutoff then gives ordinary weak C_b convergence, including nets. These steps prove local-topology continuity only on the actual established domain, not a substitute MA operator or all-PC extension on general supports.'),
dict(id='R8',statement='ALL bounded continuous obstacles satisfy the ACTUAL raw contact integral in this full affine rational-reference sector.',proof='For any u in C_b(R^d), choose finite rational PA compact-supported u_n converging locally uniformly to u with one common bound C+o(1). Construct these by rational-box grids and rational nodal value approximations on inner boxes; use an outer zero collar, then zero outside. Barycentric interpolation gives continuous rational PA on finite rational geometry with absolute bound controlled by its nodal values. This is local approximation in the explicit real/rational-denominator sector, NOT global C_b or integer-slope density.\nBy R4, f_n=P_gamma(u_n) are genuine finite rational PA PC functions with one fixed bound relative to actual gamma. R5 and the ENTIRE S272 finite-PA criterion give int(f_n-gamma-u_n) MA_raw(f_n)=0 for every n. R6 gives f_n->f=P_gamma(u) locally uniformly. The actual f is convex continuous and bounded relative to gamma, so R3 proves f in genuine GLOBAL completion before MA_raw(f) is used. R7 gives weak convergence of the genuine positive raw measures and the common fixed-bound height/tail control. The actual gaps g_n=f_n-gamma-u_n converge locally uniformly to g=f-gamma-u, with one global bound 2C+o(1). For a compact cutoff chi_R equal to one on {H0<=R} and supported on a larger sublevel, local uniform convergence and vague convergence pass int chi_R g_n MA(f_n) to int chi_R g MA(f). The tails have absolute size at most (2C+o(1))K_C/R. Let R tend to infinity. Thus int(P_gamma(u)-(gamma+u)) MA_raw(P_gamma(u))=0 for EVERY bounded continuous obstacle, with unchanged raw mass M, actual envelope and actual established operator. No normalization of PCC probabilities to raw MA mass is used.'),
dict(id='R9',statement='Scope and unresolved original requirements.',proof='This is a complete NEW UNREVIEWED working proof for full rational affine supports R^d (or a fixed rational affine isomorphism with the induced saturated lattice), all d>=1, positive constant top weight and actual RATIONAL convex PA positive-growth reference. It supplies GLOBAL genuine rational-PA regularization of all continuous PC endpoints bounded relative to that reference, finite-PA envelope recognition, the full flat-jet criterion on every refinement, and ALL bounded-continuous-obstacle raw contact. It does NOT settle arbitrary real-coefficient references with irrational recession polytopes, branched/abstract/glued/general embedded balanced supports, the complete structural iff classification, or literal integer-slope-only density. All original P05.2 remains OPEN; this working record is not a mathematical grant or accepted paper. Only accepted whole A224/B225/R230/S262/S272 with every clarification are dependencies. ROOT276/277/278/281 and new P16.4 author211/active214 are not premises. Active213/214 receive no new283 input or hot feedback. A future independent author/reviewer must reconstruct every new finite-dimensional argument, particularly R4 finite epigraph recognition and R5 quotient-line primitive calculation, before acceptance or use.')
]
